kernel sandbox (preview): auto (default); applies: off; would apply: off
  why: --allow-all with no deny rule leaves nothing to narrow
  permission set: fixed (no prompt can widen it)
  machine: [WILDLINE]
  policy [WILDLINE]
    read:       all
    deny read:  none
    write:      all
    deny write: none
    exec:       any readable program (children inherit these rules)
    load code:  all
    net:        open
    unix:       [WILDLINE]
[WILDCARD]
hello
